5:["$","section",null,{"className":"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 sm:py-20","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-3","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"lg:col-span-2","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-[var(--color-navy)] mb-6","children":["About ","Optical Express"]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-base","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Optical Express is a major UK optical and laser eye surgery provider, offering both traditional optician services and specialist refractive surgery. With clinics across the UK and Ireland, they are one of the country's largest providers of laser eye surgery and lens replacement procedures, while also offering standard high-street optical services including eye tests, glasses, and contact lenses."}],[["$","p","0",{"children":"Optical Express was founded in 1991 in Glasgow, Scotland, initially as a traditional high-street opticians chain. The company grew quickly during the 1990s, opening stores across Scotland and then expanding into England, Wales, and Northern Ireland. What distinguished Optical Express from many competitors was its early recognition of the commercial potential of laser eye surgery, which was emerging as a viable alternative to glasses and contact lenses during the same period. By the mid-1990s, Optical Express had begun investing in laser and refractive surgery services, positioning itself as both a conventional optician and a specialist surgical provider."}],["$","p","1",{"children":"The laser eye surgery division of the business grew rapidly through the 2000s, and Optical Express became one of the UK's largest providers of LASIK, LASEK, and other refractive procedures. The company invested heavily in the latest laser technology and recruited experienced ophthalmic surgeons, building a network of dedicated surgical clinics alongside its standard opticians stores. This dual model — combining everyday optical services with specialist surgery — was unusual in the UK market and gave Optical Express a distinctive niche. The company also expanded into lens replacement surgery, offering implantable contact lenses and refractive lens exchange for patients who were not suitable candidates for laser treatment."}],["$","p","2",{"children":"Today, Optical Express operates approximately 100 clinics and stores across the United Kingdom and Ireland. The business is privately owned by its founder, David Moulsdale, and employs around 2,000 people. While the laser eye surgery division generates significant revenue and attention, Optical Express continues to operate standard optician services — including NHS eye tests, glasses dispensing, and contact lens fitting — at many of its locations. The company's clinics are typically located in city centres and major towns, and it has invested in advanced diagnostic equipment including OCT scanning, corneal topography, and wavefront aberrometry across its network."}]]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-200 h-fit","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--color-navy)] mb-4","children":"Quick Facts"}],["$","dl",null,{"className":"space-y-3 text-sm","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex justify-between","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"text-gray-500","children":"Founded"}],"$L14"]}],"$L15","$L16","$L17","$L18","$L19","$L1a","$L1b"]}]]}]]}]}]
